    {
      "id": "PUB-C02",
      "title": "The graph certificate separates improvement from optimality under a fixed task.",
      "assessment": "For positive rational penalties on a finite declared graph, a feasible balanced dual circulation bounded by edge capacities gives a lower bound. Equality with an exactly checked primal cost certifies optimality. Fixed reports and gauge freedom, sparse-optimum existence versus all-optimum claims, and finite-attempt versus runtime limits are stated explicitly. Publication formatting adds no model-benefit evidence.",
