    {
      "id": "PUB-C03",
      "title": "Presentation-bound witnesses and contiguous search replay preserve the distinction between failure and obstruction.",
      "assessment": "Within the finite diagonal-sign grammar, a complete signed-graph algorithm supplies a gauge or odd closed walk. The separate bounded enumerator is a replay-control example, not a speedup result: prior candidate coverage must be checked before a resume, and a remaining suffix stays UNKNOWN. Exact matrix checking and hashing must use one immutable input snapshot. The Fock example excludes only equal-magnitude pairing of individual rooted integrated paths on its declared carrier.",
