    {
      "id": "PUB-F02",
      "title": "P3-20 drops the severity condition from diagnostic reachability.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "assessment": "Both publication ledgers say DIAGNOSTIC_ONLY is reachable exactly when derived Signal2 can disagree with Signal1 about presence. Let g(m) always report a high positive defect. At m=0 presence disagrees but the table returns DEFENSIVE_LOCKDOWN; at m>=1 it returns QUARANTINED. No diagnostic state is reachable. The full manuscript Lemma A(2) is correct: defect-only disagreement must be low/medium.",
