      "assessment": "Complete 470-line manuscript read. The finite positive-rational weighted graph model correctly separates candidate residual D from quotient minimum Phi, proves fixed-report/coboundary invariance, and uses feasible balanced capacity-bounded dual circulation plus matching objective as the optimality certificate. Cycle telescoping gives rho*abs(h); the sparse-optimum existence and sufficient weighted null-space uniqueness claims retain their quantifiers. A rank-one cycle may have an (n-1)-dimensional optimal face, so residual sparsity is not decoder sparsity. Rational strict descent needs fuel and per-attempt timeout; changing reports changes the task. Native primal cost consistency is explicitly weaker than a dual lower bound, and unpinned binaries remain trusted. Source references/Lean/native/history are prior context, not rerun here. This is useful reusable finite verification, with no claimed model accuracy benefit.",
