            ],
            "target_zero_based_slice": [
              433,
              433
            ],
            "before": "## Research extension: custody across harness replacement\r\n\r\nThe new research path adds custody identities for the experiment, candidate,\r\nparent, checker, partition, model, configuration and original budget. Raw provider\r\nbytes are retained before interpretation. A private verdict binds the submitted\r\nprogram and the actual outputs on the frozen private cases. Offline replay\r\nrechecks those outputs; it does not infer success from a stored status string.\r\nA changed reply, stale parent or substituted private case cannot inherit an\r\nexisting evaluation receipt. These are additional implementation obligations,\r\nnot claims about the historical source archive audited above.\r\n\r\nBudget custody is also persistent. Every request reserves its maximum supported\r\nliability before transport. A malformed answer may still contain valid billable\r\nusage, while a missing or ambiguous usage report retains its reservation and\r\nhalts dispatch. A child harness receives no ledger, provider credential or\r\npermission to choose its own budget identity. Experimental incumbent replacement\r\ntherefore cannot reset expenditure.\r\n\r\nA chained local journal detects inconsistent edits under a retained anchor. It\r\ndoes not authenticate a hostile host capable of replacing every object and anchor.\r\nNative executable identity, source identity and source-to-binary reproducibility\r\nremain separate claims. The live Linux containment probe and paid experiment\r\nhave not run; the new author-review package must not present local Windows tests\r\nas observations of those environments.\r\n\r\nThe source and page references for this extension are collected in\r\n[Paper 029](../029_pfp_evidence_bound_harness_evolution/paper.md) and its\r\n[source-to-claim map](../029_pfp_evidence_bound_harness_evolution/docs/source_to_claim_map.md).\r\nThe author-review rendering does not replace a historical deposit or archive.\r\n\r\n",
            "after": ""
